<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kish</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kish was an ancient Sumerian city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, associated in tradition with the first kingship after the flood. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> rose to power from service at Kish before founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a> records an early king of Kish defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a>, an episode noted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>'s profile.</p></div>
